#. Tag: title
#: formulas.docbook:11
#, no-c-format
msgid "Formulas"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: formulas.docbook:12
#, no-c-format
msgid "formulas"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formulas.docbook:14
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; has the ability to directly create formulas using the formula editor "
"common to all &koffice; applications."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formulas.docbook:15
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is a formula editor for creating graphical versions of formulas. "
"&kword; does not currently have the ability to solve mathematical equations."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: formulas.docbook:18
#, no-c-format
msgid "Add a formula"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formulas.docbook:19
#, no-c-format
msgid "There are three ways to insert a formula into a document:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formulas.docbook:22
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By selecting <menuchoice> <guimenu>Insert</guimenu><guimenuitem>Formula</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formulas.docbook:28
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using the keyboard shortcut: <keycap>F4</keycap>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formulas.docbook:32
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"or by clicking <inlinemediaobject><imageobject><imagedata fileref=\"part-"
"kformula.png\" format=\"PNG\"/></imageobject></inlinemediaobject> on the "
"toolbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formulas.docbook:37
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kword; creates a formula frame at the current cursor location."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formulas.docbook:38
#, no-c-format
msgid "Formula frames behave differently than most other frames in &kword;:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formulas.docbook:40
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<emphasis>All</emphasis> formula frames are inserted <glossterm linkend="
"\"definlineframe\">inline</glossterm> by default. This frame can later be "
"converted to a <emphasis>non-inline</emphasis> frame later."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formulas.docbook:43
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Formula frames expand and contract depending on the resulting size of the "
"formula."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formulas.docbook:44
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Formula frames automatically determine where in the line they are lined up."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: formulas.docbook:50
#, no-c-format
msgid "Moving a formula"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formulas.docbook:51
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By default, formula frames are created as <glossterm linkend=\"definlineframe"
"\">inline</glossterm> frames by default. The formula frame will move with "
"the text as any other inline frame would."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formulas.docbook:53
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want to have more control over where the formula is placed, you can "
"convert it to a framed formula by clicking on the frame surrounding the "
"formula with the &RMB;. A popup menu will appear. Simply select "
"<guilabel>Inline Frame</guilabel> and the formula will now be a freely "
"movable frame."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formulas.docbook:56
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once converted to a freely movable frame, you can <link linkend=\"move-frame"
"\">move the frame</link> just like any other frame in &kword;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: formulas.docbook:60
#, no-c-format
msgid "Removing a formula"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formulas.docbook:61
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To delete a formula in &kword;, simply <link linkend=\"delete-frame\">delete "
"the frame</link> around it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: formulas.docbook:64
#, no-c-format
msgid "Editing a formula"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formulas.docbook:65
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Editing a formula is beyond the scope of this documentation. Please see the "
"&kformula; handbook for help with the editing of the formula."
msgstr ""
